  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Newton's Method** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef optim_newtons_method(X: list, y: list, num_steps: int = 2) -> dict:\n    X_a, y_a = np.array(X, dtype=np.float64), np.array(y, dtype=np.float64)\n    N, D = X_a.shape\n    w = np.zeros(D)\n    H_inv = np.linalg.inv(np.dot(X_a.T, X_a)/N + 1e-8*np.eye(D))\n    for _ in range(int(num_steps)):\n        w -= np.dot(H_inv, np.dot(X_a.T, np.dot(X_a, w) - y_a)/N)\n    return {'weights': np.round(w, 6).tolist(), 'final_mse': round(float(np.mean((np.dot(X_a, w) - y_a)**2)), 6)}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
